@repligate You're not doing enough to distinguish between biological selection and the inference of a model from data. The inference of a model is an exact process, it either works or it doesn't. That is, there is a clear objective function (a difference in expected losses with and without a model, in the case of Bayesian statistics). The biological selection process is not exact, but a fuzzy stochastic process with many parameters, and it isn't clear what the objective function is.

